THE SONGS — ALL RIGHTS RESERVED
===============================

This directory contains song lyrics and written production, style, and audition
notes for The Final Frontier and its wider world.

Lyrics and notes © 2026 Jessica Mulein. Fully copyright Jessica Mulein and
Mulein Studios LLC.

These works are NOT open-licensed. No right to reproduce, distribute, adapt,
publicly perform, set to music, or commercially exploit them is granted, and
none should be inferred from their presence in a public repository.

This is deliberately different from the rest of the repository:

  * The novel prose, planning documents, and the audiobook narration are
    licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (see /LICENSE, section 1).
  * The build tooling is MIT (see /LICENSE, section 3).
  * These songs are reserved.

Carve-out for the novel: where the novel reproduces a passage of lyric verbatim
and as lyric, that passage stays reserved under this file. But the recurring
phrases and motifs the novel shares with the songs — "come in," "did I say yes,"
"copper and quiet," and the like — are prose under section 1 of the repository
LICENSE, and reproducing the prose that contains them needs no separate
permission.

The song RECORDINGS are not in this repository. They are published separately
under their own reserved terms. This file covers only the text stored here.

Permission for any use of these works can be requested. Ask.

